/* Terms of Use.

   Migrated verbatim from the WordPress site, which is the version the client's
   counsel signed off. Only the markup changed: WordPress emitted every section
   title as <p><strong>, so those are real h2s now and the document has an
   outline. Do not reword the text — it is a legal document, and the consent
   checkbox on every form links here.

   2026-10-19 SMS SECTION. The CTM/Twilio Trust Center requires a dedicated SMS
   section in these terms: message types, frequency, rates, STOP, HELP, that
   consent is optional, how it is collected, and sample messages that start
   with "Buena Vista Recovery:". Keep this section in step with the Privacy
   Policy, ConsentFields.astro, and /sms-consent-script.pdf. */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TopBar from '../components/TopBar.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../components/FinalCTA.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Use | Buena Vista';
const description = 'The terms that govern your use of the Buena Vista Health & Recovery Centers website.';

const content = `<p class="legal-date"><strong>Effective Date: October 19, 2026</strong></p>
<p>
Welcome to Buena Vista Health and Recovery Centers, a website owned and operated by Buena Vista Recovery, a substance use disorder treatment facility (“we,” “our,” or “us”). By accessing or using our 
<a href="/">
website
</a>
, you agree to comply with and be bound by these Terms of Use. If you do not agree with these Terms, please do not use our website.
 
</p>
<h2>Purpose of the Website</h2>
<p>
The purpose of this website is to provide general information about substance use disorder, our treatment services, and resources for individuals seeking assistance. The website may also offer contact information, educational content, and related services.
 
</p>
<p><strong>
Please note:
</strong>
 This website is not intended to provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Always seek the advice of a qualified healthcare provider with any questions you may have regarding a medical condition or treatment.
 
</p>
<h2>Eligibility</h2>
<p>
By using this website, you confirm that you are at least 18 years of age, or that you are a minor with the express consent of a parent or guardian, and that you are legally able to access and use the services provided on the site.
 
</p>
<h2>Use of Content</h2>
<p>
All content on this website, including text, graphics, images, videos, and other materials, is the property of Buena Vista Recovery or its licensors and is protected by copyright, trademark, and other intellectual property laws. You may use the content solely for personal, non-commercial purposes. Any unauthorized use of the content, including but not limited to reproduction, modification, distribution, or public display, is prohibited.
 
</p>
<h2>Medical Disclaimer</h2>
<p>
The content provided on this website is for informational purposes only and is not intended to replace professional medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. If you have or suspect you have a medical or psychological condition, please consult a qualified healthcare professional. Buena Vista Recovery does not provide medical advice through this website and is not liable for any decisions made based on information found here.
 
</p>
<h2>Privacy and Data Collection</h2>
<p>
We take your privacy seriously. Our Privacy Policy, which is incorporated into these Terms of Use, governs how we collect, use, and protect your personal information. By using this website, you consent to our practices as outlined in the Privacy Policy.
 
 
</p>
<h2>User Conduct</h2>
<p>
As a condition of your use of this Web site, you will not use the Web site or the Web site information for any purpose that is unlawful or prohibited by these Terms of Use. You will not use this Web site in any manner that could damage, disable, overload or impair the operation of this Web site or use by third parties.
 
</p>
<h2>Links to Third-Party Websites</h2>
<p>
This website may contain links to external websites or resources that are not operated or controlled by Buena Vista Recovery. We are not responsible for the content or practices of these third-party sites, and inclusion of a link does not imply endorsement. You access third-party sites at your own risk.
 
</p>
<h2>Modification of Terms</h2>
<p>
Buena Vista Recovery reserves the right to modify these Terms of Use at any time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated &#8220;Effective Date.&#8221; Your continued use of the website after any such changes will constitute your acceptance of the revised Terms.
 
</p>
<h2>SMS / Text Messages</h2>
<p>If you opt in, Buena Vista Recovery may send informational and marketing text messages (SMS, MMS, or RCS). You can expect messages such as admissions follow-ups, appointment reminders, insurance verification updates, and information about our programs and services.</p>
<p>Message frequency may vary. Message and data rates may apply.</p>
<p>You can opt out at any time by replying <strong>STOP</strong> to any message we send. You will receive one confirmation and no further texts. Reply <strong>HELP</strong> for assistance, or call <a href="tel:+18883625576">(888) 362-5576</a> or email <a href="mailto:privacy@buenavistarecovery.com">privacy@buenavistarecovery.com</a>.</p>
<p>Consent to receive text messages is optional and is not required to purchase or receive our services. We collect it in two ways, and we record your answer, the phone number, the date, and the method:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Website forms.</strong> A separate SMS checkbox that is never pre-checked, including on <a href="/about/contact/">buenavistarecovery.com/about/contact/</a> and <a href="/insurance/verify-your-benefits/">buenavistarecovery.com/insurance/verify-your-benefits/</a>. The exact language is: “By checking this box, you provide consent to receive informational and marketing SMS, MMS, or RCS messages from Buena Vista Recovery. Message frequency may vary. Message and data rates may apply. Reply HELP for help or STOP to opt out.”</li>
<li><strong>Verbal consent.</strong> An admissions representative at <a href="tel:+18883625576">(888) 362-5576</a> reads this script and records your answer: “Would you like to receive texts from Buena Vista Recovery? Message frequency may vary. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out or HELP for help. No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes. Agreeing is optional and is not required to receive our services.” The script is published at <a href="/sms-consent-script.pdf">buenavistarecovery.com/sms-consent-script.pdf</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes. All the above categories exclude text messaging originator opt-in data and consent; this information will not be shared with any third parties.</p>
<h3>Sample messages</h3>
<p>Messages we send include these disclosures, and our opt-in confirmation and HELP replies begin with our business name:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Sample message:</strong> Buena Vista Recovery: Thanks for contacting us about treatment. We will follow up on your inquiry. Message frequency may vary. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out. Reply HELP for help.</li>
<li><strong>Sample message:</strong> Buena Vista Recovery: This is a reminder about your admissions appointment. Message frequency may vary. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out. Reply HELP for help.</li>
<li><strong>Opt-in confirmation:</strong> Buena Vista Recovery: You are opted in to receive texts from us. Message frequency may vary. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out. Reply HELP for help.</li>
<li><strong>HELP reply:</strong> Buena Vista Recovery: For help, call (888) 362-5576 or email privacy@buenavistarecovery.com. Message frequency may vary. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out.</li>
</ul>
